etting up the Workflow (one-time)
In the Teams channel you want alerts posted to, click ... next to the channel name → Workflows.
Search for and select "Post to a channel when a webhook request is received."
Authenticate, then choose the Team and Channel to post into → Add workflow.
It'll generate a unique HTTP POST URL — copy that into TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL in the script.
This is the step that matters: open the flow in Power Automate (Workflows app → your flow → Edit), expand the "When a Teams webhook request is received" trigger, and use "Use sample payload to generate schema." Paste in the contents of teams_workflow_sample_payload.json above. This teaches the trigger that the request body has an attachments array — without this, the auto-generated "for each attachment" / "post card" steps downstream will fail with a null-array error even though your actual POST is fine.
Power Automate should auto-build the rest of the flow (a "for each" over attachments → "post card in a chat or channel," referencing the card content dynamically). Save it.
Test: run the script once with TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL set, or just curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d @teams_workflow_sample_payload.json "<your-url>" — should post the card immediately.

One thing worth knowing going in: this trigger type explicitly does not support actionable buttons ("actions" blocks) in the card — only display content works. My card doesn't use any, so you're fine as-is, but if you later want "Acknowledge" / "View table" buttons on the alert, that won't work through this webhook trigger and would need a different setup (an actual bot registration).

